                "Let us architect the 4-Phase Blameless Postmortem Narrative Framework: 1. Incident Timeline & Blast Radius ($20\\text{ to }25\\text{ seconds}$): State the technical context, the unexpected trigger, and the exact customer or business impact ('At 2:15 PM on a Tuesday, our cache invalidation worker experienced a race condition, causing our Redis cluster memory to spike to 100% and taking down our API for 18 minutes, dropping approximately 12,000 requests'); 2. Immediate Triage & Mitigation ($20\\text{ to }25\\text{ seconds}$): Describe how you kept your head cool, prioritized restoring uptime over assigning blame, and executed immediate remediation ('Rather than debating why the script failed on Slack, I immediately hopped onto the incident bridge, initiated our disaster recovery runbook, shifted traffic to our secondary cluster, and restored API availability within 8 minutes'); 3. Root Cause Analysis ($30\\text{ to }40\\text{ seconds}$): Deconstruct the technical mechanism of the failure down to its architectural origins using first principles; 4. Systemic Prevention Guardrails ($30\\text{ to }40\\text{ seconds}$): Describe the permanent tooling, linting rules, architectural patterns, and monitoring alerts you instituted so this failure class can NEVER happen again.",
